    description: ""  # aeb7
    fields:  # aeb7
      statement: "When multiple Go files define the same symbol (same package name, same function), call resolution must use the import path to pick the correct target file"  # aeb7
      root_cause: "`symbol_resolution.py:ListNameResolver.lookup()` only checked the last directory segment of the import path (e.g., \"genproto\") which matched multiple candidates. When no unique match was found, it returned the first candidate, which was non-deterministic across Python versions."  # aeb7
      fix: "Enhanced `ListNameResolver.lookup()` to: 1. Try progressively shorter suffixes of the import path (e.g., \"zzz_correct/genproto\", \"genproto\") 2. Return when exactly one candidate matches a suffix 3. Sort candidates deterministically (by path) when falling back to ambiguous resolution"  # aeb7
      regression_tests:  # aeb7
      - tests/test_go.py::TestGoImportPathResolution::test_resolves_call_to_correct_file_by_import_path  # aeb7
